Schubert calculus is the study of linear spaces having special position with respect to fixed but general linear spaces.
We provide background and describe a series of surprising conjectures and theorems about real solutions to problems in Schubert calculus.
Large computations played a big role in uncovering conjectures and motivating theorems in this area.

