The first implementation now builds and verifies across all four presets. At the initial shipping preset, the intended residue-square recovery takes 246 exact operations, while the generic modular factorizer took about 1.8 million counted field operations on the first benchmark instance—enough separation for Track B. I’m running the full 200,000-sample and eight-seed adversary suite now; any attack success or reference failure will force a redesign.
