+"""Exact Wronskian-factor generator for arXiv:1307.1833.
+
+The paper identifies a k-plane of polynomials with its projective Wronskian.
+This module asks for the exact roots and multiplicities of that Wronskian.
+Instances are built from a common quadratic times an arithmetic progression of
+powers of one shifted coordinate, followed by an invertible basis change.  The
+certificate follows from W(r f_1,...,r f_k)=r^k W(f_1,...,f_k) and the
+Wronskian-of-monomials identity; no generated instance is solved to obtain it.
+"""
